# Shell

::summary
ONE source of shell truth for the web mockup: a SINGLE responsive sidebar-main-panel shell (240px sidebar with wordmark, five surface rows (Search, Docs, Tasks, Apps, Messages), divider, hub group — collapsing to a 68px icon rail at medium and a renderer-generated bottom tab-bar at small, with Surfy staying top-right in the top bar rather than becoming a FAB), top bar, right-docked Surfy panel with the dropdown-select tier switcher. Shell-owned sheets live in `modals/` (hub, workspace-switcher, surfy-chats) — this file defines no modals. Surface files under `surfaces/` compose per the wrapper ruling below.
::

## Composition ruling — how surfaces compose with this shell

The `shell=` attribute has NO engine support — it was a fiction and is retired. RULED here (R-A, 08-10): there is **ONE responsive shell** — no separate narrow source. **Each surface file inlines its own `::app-shell` wrapper**, copied VERBATIM from the shell in this file — sidebar (wordmark + five surface rows + divider + hub group), top bar, then a single `tab-content` pane holding the surface body one nesting level deeper. The pane is NAMED for the owning surface row — `tab=docs` / `tab=tasks` / `tab=apps` / `tab=messages` (detail surfaces name their parent list's tab; hub-owned surfaces, whose rows sit below the divider, keep `tab=main`). At small widths the renderer GENERATES the bottom tab-bar from the sidebar's surface nav rows (the live /next renderer then reorders Search LAST, matching the iOS compact tab-bar roster Docs · Tasks · Apps · Messages · Search) — label and the unread dot derive from each row and its `unread` attr; the ACTIVE item is the row whose title slug matches the shell's initially active tab pane (else the first item — the renderer cannot express "none active", so hub-owned surfaces show Docs highlighted; known 0.14.0 gap). The retired hand-authored tabs shell is gone. Rules of the idiom:

- This file is the SINGLE POINT OF EDIT for chrome. When the shell changes, every surface wrapper is regenerated from here; surface files never fork chrome content.
- The wrapper's sidebar marks the owning surface's row `state=active` (detail surfaces mark their parent list's row).
- The ruled 880px centered column (Docs and Apps lists, and detail surfaces) is expressed as `width=880 align=center` on the surface's `tab-content`. Surfaces that RELEASE the column (Messages split view, Tasks board scrollport) omit those attrs.
- Surface wrappers render with the Surfy panel CLOSED — they omit `:::panel`. The open-panel truth (tier switcher, chats button, composer) lives ONLY in the shell source below; a surface reviewed with the panel open is a shell state, not a surface state.
- `app-shell` takes `height=` per surface to avoid the clamp clipping long pages (app detail, task detail).
- Shell-owned sheets are referenced by stable name, never redefined: `modals/hub.surf` (name=hub), `modals/workspace-switcher.surf` (name=workspace-switcher), `modals/surfy-chats.surf` (name=surfy-chats).

